sequenceDiagram
  participant User as Staff / Student
  participant BFF as Next.js BFF
  participant Client as Staff API client
  participant API as Spring Identity API
  participant DB as PostgreSQL
  alt Browser sign-in for an account without MFA
    User->>BFF: Login credentials over HTTPS
    BFF->>API: POST /auth/login
    API->>DB: Check password, account status and lockout
    API-->>BFF: Access JWT and opaque refresh token
    BFF-->>User: HttpOnly SameSite session cookies
    User->>BFF: Protected request with session cookie
    Note over User,BFF: BFF checks Origin on mutations
    BFF->>API: Bearer JWT on server-side request
  else Owner or administrator sign-in through the API
    User->>Client: Login credentials
    Client->>API: POST /auth/login
    API->>DB: Check password and store challenge digest
    API-->>Client: MFA challenge with enrolment status
    opt First sign-in or authenticator reset
      Client->>API: POST /auth/mfa/enroll with challenge
      API->>DB: Store encrypted authenticator secret
      API-->>Client: Setup secret and authenticator URI
    end
    User->>Client: Authenticator or recovery code
    Client->>API: POST /auth/mfa/verify with challenge and code
    API->>DB: Verify factor, consume challenge and start MFA session
    API-->>Client: Access JWT, refresh token and recovery codes on enrolment
    Client->>API: Protected request with bearer JWT
  end
  API->>API: Check token, session, privileged MFA, roles and resource scope
  Note over BFF,API: Refresh rotates the opaque token and reuse revokes the session
